#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "General settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of columns to show"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Folders are automatically distributed in several columns. The optimal number "
"of "
"columns depends on the width of the konqueror window and the number of "
"bookmarks you have."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show folder backgrounds"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disable it on slow system to disable background images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show bookmarks without folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is unchecked, bookmarks at the root of the hierarchy (not in a "
"folder) are not displayed. If checked, they are gathered in a \"root\" folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Flatten bookmarks tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sub-folders are shown within their parent by default. If you activate this "
"option, sub-folders are displayed on their own. It looks less nice but it may "
"help if you have a very big folder you want to spread in two columns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show system places"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show a box with KDE places (Home, Network, ...). Useful if you use konqueror "
"as "
"a file manager."
msgstr ""

